(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching a Qubit: Continuous Measurement and Quantum Trajectories\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["A live, computation-first walk through the diffusive \
stochastic master equation of a continuously monitored qubit in the Wolfram \
Language: the deterministic Lindblad equation describes the ensemble that \
ignores the detector, while conditioning the state on a homodyne readout \
unravels it into individual stochastic quantum trajectories; a \
positivity-preserving integrator, built from plain matrices, turns each \
detector record into a trajectory; and averaging the trajectories over the \
measurement noise recovers the Lindblad state, with measurement-induced \
dephasing, spontaneous-emission diffusion, a two-point correlation of the \
readout current, inefficient detection, and a qutrit all read off cells you \
can rerun.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami. Last updated July 29, 2026.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook tells one story as a continuous sequence: what it means to \
watch a quantum system weakly and continuously, how that watching turns the \
deterministic Lindblad master equation into a stochastic master equation \
(SME) for the state conditioned on the detector's record, how a single \
positivity-preserving update rule integrates the SME from plain matrices, and \
how the same map, run over and over, reproduces measurement-induced \
dephasing, spontaneous-emission diffusion, the two-point statistics of the \
homodyne current, and, once the map is dimension-general and \
efficiency-aware, inefficient detection and a qutrit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, \
if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. So almost nothing \
here is asserted without a cell that computes it on the spot, and almost \
every claim is checked against an independent calculation, an ensemble \
average against a master-equation solution, or a positivity test against the \
scheme's promise.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
This is a live Wolfram notebook, not a static paper. Evaluate the cells top \
to bottom; each cell holds one computation and depends on symbols defined \
earlier, so a fresh kernel wants a fresh top-to-bottom pass. Read it as a \
movie rather than a reference: each cell sets up the next question, and the \
prose between cells is the connective tissue, not decoration. My suggestion \
is to focus on each output and its meaning before worrying about every detail \
of the input. And remember that the code is yours: change the measurement \
strength, the drive, the initial state, the number of trajectories, rerun, \
and see what moves.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The integrator, the object this notebook is really about, is a short \
function over plain complex matrices with no dependency on the \
QuantumFramework paclet. Two convenience pieces come from the Wolfram \
Function Repository: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " integrates the unconditional master equation we check the trajectories \
against, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " draws the sphere. Both install automatically the first time you evaluate \
them, so the first run needs a network connection. Prerequisites are light: \
basic quantum mechanics (states, density matrices, the Pauli operators) and \
enough Wolfram Language to read a one-line function. No stochastic calculus \
is needed beyond one fact, stated when we first use it: over a step of length \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " the Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " is a zero-mean Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ". Throughout we work in natural units with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ", so Hamiltonians are measured in frequency and rates and times are \
reciprocal."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Part I: Two Descriptions of a Monitored Qubit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the object every open-system calculation begins from. A quantum \
system coupled to an environment, and left unobserved, has a state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " (a density matrix) that obeys the Lindblad master equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
         StyleBox["c", "TI"]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}], ","}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " is the Hamiltonian, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " are the jump (Lindblad) operators through which the environment acts, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " is the dissipator (the superoperator that carries irreversible loss; the \
anticommutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " keeps the trace fixed). In words: this is the equation for the state of a \
system whose environment is there but not being watched, and it is \
deterministic and smooth. Its solution is the ",
 StyleBox["unconditional", "TI"],
 " state, the average over everything the environment could have done."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now change one thing: put a detector on one of those channels. Suppose an \
experimenter monitors the system through a jump operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 ", for instance by collecting the light it scatters and mixing it with a \
local oscillator (homodyne detection). The detector returns a continuous, \
noisy signal, and the state of the system, given that signal, is no longer \
the smooth unconditional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ". It is a ",
 StyleBox["conditional", "TI"],
 " state that jitters with the record. Splitting the jump operators into \
monitored ones ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " (with detector efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 ") and unmonitored ones ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " (environment we cannot see), the conditional state obeys the diffusive ",
 StyleBox["stochastic master equation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "\[ThickSpace]", "\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThickSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the measurement superoperator (the innovation term) ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ", and each detector emitting a readout increment"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, the SME is the master equation plus one stochastic term per \
monitored channel: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " nudges the state toward agreement with the reading, weighted by the Wiener \
increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ", which is the detector's shot noise. That same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " appears in the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 ", so the record is signal (the mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 ") buried in noise, and the state can be reconstructed from the record. The \
rates are folded into the operators throughout, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[LeftArrow]", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 ", so a monitored channel of rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and unit coupling is passed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 "; this is the convention the code below expects."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two limits are worth naming before we compute. If no channel is monitored, \
every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " and the SME collapses back to the Lindblad master equation: the unwatched \
state. And if we run the SME for many independent noise realizations and \
average, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " terms average to zero (a Wiener increment has zero mean), so the mean \
conditional state obeys the master equation again. This is the single most \
important fact in the subject, and we will verify it directly: ",
 StyleBox["one trajectory is stochastic and, at unit efficiency, pure; the \
average of many trajectories is the deterministic, generally mixed, \
master-equation state.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " We will return to the readout ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " in Part VI, where it becomes the object of study."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One subtlety underlies everything that follows, so state it plainly. The \
only thing a detector ",
 StyleBox["directly", "TI"],
 " produces is the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 ": one real, noisy number per time step. The conditional state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 ", and therefore its Bloch vector, its purity, and every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " we will plot from a single run, is not itself measured but ",
 StyleBox["inferred", "TI"],
 ", and the SME is exactly the optimal filter that does the inferring: it is \
the quantum analogue of a Kalman filter, turning the record into the \
observer's best estimate of the state. So when a plot below shows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " for one trajectory, read it as a quantity an experimenter reconstructs by \
feeding a recorded current through this same equation, not as a raw meter \
reading. ",
 StyleBox["The record is the observable; the state, and everything computed \
from it, is what you infer from the record.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " That is why Part VI, which analyzes the record directly, is where the \
essay finally touches measured data, and why the menu of things one can do \
with a record (estimate the state, its spectrum, the system's parameters, or \
a feedback signal) is worth laying out once we have one in hand."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["Part II: A Positivity-Preserving Update", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A naive Euler step of the SME can push ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " to a matrix with a negative eigenvalue, an unphysical state, especially at \
large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ". The scheme we use avoids this by construction. Over one step it forms an ",
 StyleBox["unnormalized", "TI"],
 " conditional state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " and divides it by its own trace,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "=", 
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", "1", "-", 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[ThickSpace]", "+", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[ThickSpace]", "+", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]}],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"r", "s"}], "TI"]], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ". This positivity-preserving update is based on a paper of Rouchon and \
Ralph, ",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:1410.5345",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.5345"], None}],
 ". In words: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " is a sum of terms of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ", and any such sum is positive semidefinite whenever ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " is, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 " is a valid unnormalized state at ",
 StyleBox["any", "TI"],
 " step size, and dividing by its trace ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " restores unit trace. The unmonitored channels and the unmonitored fraction \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " of each detector re-enter as ordinary dissipators, the light that leaks \
away unrecorded."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The paper keeps that double sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"r", "s"}], "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 "; the code groups it into a single square. Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 ", the scalar increments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " factor out, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " identically (the operator order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " is preserved), while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"r", "s"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " diagonal contributes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 ". The double sum is therefore exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ", an algebraic identity valid for any number of monitored operators, not an \
approximation, so"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"e", "f", "f"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"c", "o", "r", "r"}], "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"e", "f", "f"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"i", "H"}], "TI"], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         RowBox[{
          UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
           StyleBox["r", "TI"],
           LimitsPositioning->False], 
          RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]}]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         RowBox[{
          UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
           StyleBox["j", "TI"],
           LimitsPositioning->False], 
          RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]}]}]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        FontSize->1.8 Inherited]}], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"c", "o", "r", "r"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", "2"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"c", "o", "r", "r"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " is the Ito correction. This grouped form is algebraically identical to the \
double-sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["M", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " above, and it is the form the code builds. Everything that does not change \
from step to step (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"e", "f", "f"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"c", "o", "r", "r"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 ") is computed once, and the per-step work is one readout, one contraction \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 ", and one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Begin with the readout increments of one step, the vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "y"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " with one entry per monitored operator. This is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalR]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ": it takes the current state, the monitored operators, the step, the Wiener \
draws ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "w"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 ", and the efficiencies, and returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", ",", " ", "\[ScriptCapitalT]"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Rho]_", ",", " ", "Ls_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "dw_", ",", " ", 
     "\[Eta]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#3", "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
           " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "#2"}], " ", 
      "&"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Ls", ",", " ", "dw", ",", " ", "\[Eta]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the trajectory map itself. This is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 ": given an initial density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rho]0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 ", a Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData["H"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ", a list of monitored operators ",
 Cell[BoxData["Ls"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " (already scaled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 "), optional efficiencies ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Eta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 " and unmonitored operators ",
 Cell[BoxData["V"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 ", a step ",
 Cell[BoxData["dt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", and a final time ",
 Cell[BoxData["tf"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 ", it returns the list of conditioned density matrices, one per time point, \
and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 "s the readout vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "y"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " at every step so a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reap"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " around the call recovers the record. Read it as the collapsed scheme \
above: precompute ",
 Cell[BoxData["heff"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["lcorr"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 ", draw all the noise at once, and fold the per-step update ",
 Cell[BoxData["step"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " over the noise with ",
 Cell[BoxData["FoldList"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]0_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"H_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", "Ls_List", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"None", " ", "|", " ", "_List"}], ")"}], " ", ":", " ", 
      "None"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"V", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"None", " ", "|", " ", "_List"}], ")"}], " ", ":", " ", 
      "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"r0", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Hn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "H", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Lsn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "Ls", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dtn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "dt", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", "\[Eta]v", ",", 
       " ", "Vsn", ",", " ", "heff", ",", " ", "lcorr", ",", " ", "nsteps", ",",
        " ", "dw", ",", " ", "step"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{"If", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "Ls", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\[Eta]"}],
          "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Vsn", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"If", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"V", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"N", "[", "V", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"heff", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"I", " ", "Hn"}], "\n", "       ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Lsn"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
           "       ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Vsn"}], "]"}]}]}], 
          ")"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"lcorr", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"dtn", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"#2", " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Eta]v", ",", " ", "Lsn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"nsteps", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"dw", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dtn", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "Lsn", "]"}], ",", " ", "nsteps"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"step", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]_", ",", " ", "dwv_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"dy", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "num"}], 
          "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dy", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sow", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "\[Rho]", ",", " ", "Lsn", ",", " ", "dtn", ",", " ", "dwv", ",",
               " ", "\[Eta]v"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
            RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#2", "]"}], " ", "#3"}], " ", "&"}], ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"dy", ",", " ", "\[Eta]v", ",", " ", "Lsn"}], "}"}]}], 
             "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"heff", " ", "+", " ", "s", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"s", " ", ".", " ", "s"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "lcorr"}]}], 
          ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"num", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "\n", 
            "          ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ",
                 "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Vsn"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "          ", 
            "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"#1", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}]}],
                  " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"Lsn", ",", " ", "\[Eta]v"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"num", "/", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "num", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
       RowBox[{"step", ",", " ", "r0", ",", " ", "dw"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A few design choices are worth reading off the code. The inputs are \
numericalized once up front (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"N", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"N", "[", "H", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"N", "[", "Ls", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 "), so passing exact matrices like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 " costs nothing and the hot loop runs on packed numeric arrays. Nothing in \
the body refers to any external paclet: ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rho]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["H"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 ", and the operators are ordinary dense complex matrices. The dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData["d"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " is read from the state, so the same function runs a qubit, a qutrit, or \
two qubits without change, which is the freedom Part VII spends. And the \
pattern guards (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"_", "?", "MatrixQ"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["_List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"None", " ", "|", " ", "_List"}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ") let the two middle arguments be optional while keeping the call \
unambiguous, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "tf"}],
    "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "\[Eta]", ",", " ", 
    "V", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "tf"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " both parse correctly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell["\<\
Next the primitives everything is built from. Define the Pauli matrices and \
the identity:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Y", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Z", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Id", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The qubit lowering operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ". Define it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"X", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "Y"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "See what it does: display ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " as a matrix and its action on the two basis states:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<J\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\< = \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", "Jminus", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<J\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<|0\[RightAngleBracket] = \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<J\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<|1\[RightAngleBracket] = \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"], "=", "(", GridBox[{
     {"0", "0"},
     {"1", "0"}
    }], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 " sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " and annihilates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ". Note the convention this fixes: here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 " is the ",
 StyleBox["upper", "TI"],
 " state that decays and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 " is the ground (dark) state, so spontaneous emission through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 " drives the qubit toward ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 ". Some literature labels these the other way; we will keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " excited throughout."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A density matrix is the outer product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " of a state vector with its conjugate. Define that map:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell["\<\
Name the three basis states we will start from, the excited state, the ground \
state, and the equatorial superposition:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ket0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ket1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ketPlus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Show the density matrices of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<|0\[RightAngleBracket]\[LeftAngleBracket]0| = \>\"", ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ket0", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<|+\[RightAngleBracket]\[LeftAngleBracket]+| = \>\"", ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, the geometry. A qubit state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " is fully described by its Bloch vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "A"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 ", real because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " and the Paulis are Hermitian. Define the Bloch-vector extractor:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 " sits at the north pole ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
  RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ket0", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the sphere itself we use the Function Repository resource ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 ": called with no argument, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " draws an empty Bloch sphere, onto which we overlay each run's full Bloch \
trajectory as a curve with ",
 Cell[BoxData["Show"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 ". That is the entire toolkit: the map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 ", the readout ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalR]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 ", the primitives, the Bloch vector, and the sphere plotter. Everything \
below is these with a different Hamiltonian, jump operator, or efficiency."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell["\<\
Part III: The Lindblad Limit: One Noisy Run and the Average of Many\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall the central claim of Part I: one trajectory is stochastic, but the \
average of many is the deterministic master-equation state. This Part checks \
it directly, on the simplest interesting case, a driven qubit whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " is continuously measured, with the Hamiltonian a Rabi drive about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " and the monitored operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " at a rate large compared with the drive. Fix the drive, the monitored \
operator, the initial state, the step, and the horizon:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"H", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "X"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Ls", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ket0", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]t", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "20.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To have something to compare the ensemble against, we need the \
unconditional (Lindblad) solution. The Function Repository's ",
 Cell[BoxData["LindbladSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " integrates the master equation from the Hamiltonian, the jump operators, \
and the initial state, returning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " as an interpolating function. Solve it for this scenario:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lind", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tf"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell["Set the time grid the trajectories will use:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tgrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]t", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tf", "/", "\[Delta]t"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell["\<\
Read the Lindblad Bloch trajectory off the interpolating solution:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindBloch", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
      RowBox[{"lind", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "tgrid"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell["\<\
Now one conditioned run. Generate one trajectory on a fixed seed so the \
picture is reproducible:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "\[Delta]t", ",", 
       " ", "tf"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell["Extract its Bloch trajectory:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneBloch", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", "oneRun"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell["\<\
Before plotting, cash in the promise of the scheme: every state in the run \
should be a legitimate density matrix. Check that all of them are positive \
semidefinite:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Tally", "[", 
  RowBox[{"PositiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", " ", "/@", " ", "oneRun"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every state passes, which is the scheme's positivity guarantee made \
concrete: the numerator is a sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " terms, so positivity never fails, here or at any step size. Now overlay \
the single conditioned ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 " on the smooth Lindblad ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"oneBloch", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lindBloch", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<one trajectory \:27e8Z\:27e9\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Lindblad \:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<One monitored run jitters around the smooth master-equation \
curve\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the single trajectory fluctuates continuously while the \
Lindblad curve slides smoothly downward. The strong ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " measurement pins the qubit near a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " eigenstate and only slowly lets the drive tip it over, so both curves \
decay gently rather than oscillating (we will contrast this with the \
weak-measurement regime in Part IV). The trajectory is one realization of the \
detector's noise; the Lindblad curve is what remains when the noise is \
averaged away. To make that precise, average many trajectories. Run an \
ensemble of 200 conditioned trajectories on a fixed seed:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ensemble", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "\[Delta]t", ",", 
         " ", "tf"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "200", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell["Average them into the mean state at each time:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "ensemble", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell["Read its Bloch trajectory:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanBloch", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", "meanStates"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare the ensemble mean of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " against the Lindblad prediction:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"meanBloch", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lindBloch", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<mean of 200 trajectories \:27e8Z\:27e9\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Lindblad \:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<200 trajectories average to the master equation\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell["Report the largest discrepancy across the whole trajectory:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"meanBloch", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"lindBloch", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean tracks the Lindblad curve, and the residual sits at the \
Monte-Carlo scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.07"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "200"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 " realizations; push ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 " higher and it shrinks as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],
 ". This is the trajectory unravelling of the master equation made numerical: \
the smooth, deterministic Lindblad state is nothing but the average over \
these jittering conditioned runs, each of which is a state an experimenter \
could actually infer from a detector record. The next question is what the \
individual runs look like when the drive, not the measurement, dominates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell["\<\
Part IV: Fast versus Slow Monitoring: Measurement-Induced Dephasing\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The comparison that makes continuous measurement vivid is strong versus \
weak monitoring of the same driven qubit. Recall the Bloch equations for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", "\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " measured: the drive rotates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 " into each other at frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ", while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " dissipator damps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 ". The ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " decides which wins. Keep the drive fixed and take two rates, one well \
above and one well below it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]d", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Hd", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]d", " ", "X"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0d", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ket0", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]td", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfd", " ", "=", " ", "20.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]Fast", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]Slow", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["Set the shared time grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tgridd", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]td", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tfd", "/", "\[Delta]td"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell["\<\
First the master-equation view, which is deterministic and needs no \
averaging. Solve Lindblad at the fast rate:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindFast", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hd", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]Fast", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", "\[Rho]0d", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tfd"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 " on the grid:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zFast", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
       RowBox[{"lindFast", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "tgridd"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell["Solve Lindblad at the slow rate:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindSlow", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hd", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]Slow", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", "\[Rho]0d", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tfd"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zSlow", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
       RowBox[{"lindSlow", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "tgridd"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell["Plot the two unconditional curves together:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgridd", ",", " ", "zFast"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgridd", ",", " ", "zSlow"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Gamma] = 2 \[GreaterGreater] \[CapitalOmega] (frozen)\>\"",
       ",", " ", "\"\<\[Gamma] = 0.1 \[LessLess] \[CapitalOmega] \
(Rabi)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Strong measurement freezes the qubit; weak measurement lets it \
oscillate\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two regimes could hardly look more different. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[GreaterGreater]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 " the qubit is nearly frozen: strong ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],
 " monitoring keeps collapsing it back toward a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 " eigenstate faster than the drive can rotate it away, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " decays slowly and monotonically at the Zeno rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 ". This is the quantum Zeno effect: watching a system in a basis suppresses \
the coherent evolution out of that basis. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[LessLess]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 " the drive wins and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 " executes Rabi oscillations at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 ", their envelope slowly eroded by the weak dephasing at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell["\<\
The trajectory view shows the same physics one record at a time. Take one \
conditioned run at the fast rate:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"runFast", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]0d", ",", " ", "Hd", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]Fast", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "\[Delta]td", ",", " ", "tfd"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell["And one at the slow rate, on the same seed:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"runSlow", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]0d", ",", " ", "Hd", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]Slow", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "\[Delta]td", ",", " ", "tfd"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlay their ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgridd", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "runFast"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tgridd", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "runSlow"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.7", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.7", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Gamma] = 2 trajectory\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Gamma] = 0.1 trajectory\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<One record apiece: frozen near \[PlusMinus]1, or noisily \
oscillating\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The strongly measured run clings near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 ", taking rare, quick excursions as the drive occasionally flips it: the \
record is telling the experimenter, most of the time, which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 " eigenstate the qubit is in. The weakly measured run instead follows the \
Rabi oscillation, dressed in noise, because each weak reading barely perturbs \
the coherent motion. Same drive, same detector, opposite behavior, set \
entirely by how hard we look."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell["Part V: Spontaneous Emission: Diffusion on the Bloch Sphere", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now let the monitored channel be spontaneous emission rather than \
dephasing, so the jump operator is the lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 ". Homodyne detection of the emitted field gives a diffusive unravelling, \
and the conditioned state wanders continuously over the Bloch sphere instead \
of jumping. Take a driven, detuned qubit emitting at a modest rate, started \
on the equator:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]s", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]s", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Hs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]s", " ", "X"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]s", " ", "Z"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]s", " ", "=", " ", "0.2"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Lse", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]s", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0s", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]ts", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfs", " ", "=", " ", "10.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],

Cell["Set the time grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tgrids", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]ts", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tfs", "/", "\[Delta]ts"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The unconditional state decays toward the ground state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 " while the drive stirs it. Solve its master equation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"Hs", ",", " ", "Lse", ",", " ", "\[Rho]0s", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tfs"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell["Read its Bloch trajectory:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindBlochS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
      RowBox[{"lindS", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "tgrids"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell["\<\
Individual trajectories show the diffusion directly. Generate a handful of \
conditioned runs and take their full Bloch trajectories:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fewRuns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "\[Rho]0s", ",", " ", "Hs", ",", " ", "Lse", ",", " ", "\[Delta]ts", 
          ",", " ", "tfs"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "5", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Draw the sphere with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"BlochSpherePlot", "[", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 " and overlay each run's full trajectory as a curve:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
            RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"First", "@", "#2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Line", "@", "#1"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
        "fewRuns"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "420"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, each conditioned run traces its own wandering curve over the \
sphere, drifting in from the equatorial start toward the ground-state pole as \
the qubit emits, and no two curves coincide because each is driven by its own \
detector noise. This is measurement-induced diffusion: the homodyne record \
continuously reshapes the state, and the spread of the curves is the spread \
of possible records. Now average many of them and confirm the mean returns \
the master equation. Run an ensemble of 200 trajectories:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ensembleS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "\[Rho]0s", ",", " ", "Hs", ",", " ", "Lse", ",", " ", "\[Delta]ts", ",",
          " ", "tfs"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "200", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell["Read the mean Bloch trajectory:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanBlochS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "ensembleS", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the three ensemble-mean components against the Lindblad prediction:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tgrids", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "meanBlochS", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tgrids", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "lindBlochS", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Black"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Bloch components\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"SwatchLegend", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Black"}], "}"}], ",",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<\:27e8X\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\:27e8Y\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\:27e8Z\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Lindblad (all three)\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<200 emission trajectories average to the master equation, all \
three components\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell["\<\
The three ensemble means fall on the three dashed Lindblad curves to \
Monte-Carlo scatter: the diffusing pure trajectories, averaged, reconstruct \
the decaying mixed state exactly as in Part III, now for an amplitude-damping \
channel rather than dephasing.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell["Reproducing Wiseman and Milburn, Figure 4.6", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A classic picture of a single homodyne trajectory plots its angles on the \
sphere: the azimuth ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", 
   StyleBox["arctan",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 ". Take the resonant, undetuned drive of the textbook figure and its \
emission channel:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]w", " ", "=", " ", "3.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Hw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]w", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Y", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]w", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Lw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]w", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0w", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]tw", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfw", " ", "=", " ", "10.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell["Generate one trajectory's Bloch record:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"trajW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Rho]0w", ",", " ", "Hw", ",", " ", "Lw", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tw", ",",
         " ", "tfw"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot its azimuth ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ArcTan", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "#3"}], "}"}], " ", 
      "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", "trajW"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[CurlyPhi] = arctan(\:27e8Y\:27e9,\:27e8X\:27e9)\>\"", ",",
       " ", "\"\<cos \[Theta] = \:27e8Z\:27e9\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<step\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<angle\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A single homodyne trajectory: azimuth \[CurlyPhi] and polar cos \
\[Theta]\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement phase is itself a knob: mixing the emitted field with a \
local oscillator shifted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],
 " multiplies the monitored operator by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],
 ", so a different quadrature of the field is recorded. Rotate the measured \
quadrature:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Lw2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]w", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell["Rerun with the same seed:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"trajW2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Rho]0w", ",", " ", "Hw", ",", " ", "Lw2", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tw", ",",
         " ", "tfw"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],

Cell["Plot its angles:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ArcTan", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "#3"}], "}"}], " ", 
      "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", "trajW2"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[CurlyPhi]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<cos \[Theta]\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<step\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<angle\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Rotating the measured quadrature by \[Pi]/2 changes the \
trajectory\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[48]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],

Cell["\<\
Same qubit, same drive, same seed, but the recorded quadrature is different, \
and so is the path the state takes: the trajectory is a property of the \
measurement as much as of the system.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell["Part VI: The Measurement Record", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So far we have read the conditioned ",
 StyleBox["state", "TI"],
 " off each run. But Part I was blunt about what an experiment directly \
records: only the ",
 StyleBox["current", "TI"],
 ", the readout increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 ", which ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],
 " has been ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],
 "-ing all along. The Bloch vectors and purities of Parts III through V were \
never measured; they were inferred from a record by the SME. This Part works \
with the record itself: first its two-point correlation, then its power \
spectrum, then the honest question the framing forces, whether the inferred \
single-run trajectories were ever real. That analysis needs a long record, so \
set a resonantly driven, emitting qubit and a long horizon:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]c", " ", "=", " ", "3.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Hc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]c", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Y", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]c", " ", "=", " ", "0.7"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Lc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]c", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0c", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ket0", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]tc", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfc", " ", "=", " ", "4000.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[49]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],

Cell["Generate the trajectory and reap the readout it sows:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"trajC", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "records", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reap", "@", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Rho]0c", ",", " ", "Hc", ",", " ", "Lc", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc", ",",
         " ", "tfc"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[50]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],

Cell["\<\
There is only one monitored operator, so there is one current. Pull out its \
time series:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"current", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "records", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[51]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell["Check its length:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "current", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[52]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],

Cell["A Two-Point Correlation of the Raw Record", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One step of the record is signal plus noise, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],
 ": the signal is of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 ", while the shot noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],
 " has standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 ", so at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0.01"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],
 " each sample is about ten parts noise to one part signal. Confirm the \
record is noise-dominated sample by sample:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "current", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "current", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Delta]tc", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[53]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The standard deviation is essentially ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "0.1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 ", so one reading tells you almost nothing. The two-point correlation asks a \
different question, whether the reading at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 " is statistically related to the reading a lag ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " later, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "R"}], "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 ". It is worth computing for a modest reason: coherent dynamics leave a \
fingerprint in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],
 " that survives the shot noise, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 " is the step toward the power spectrum a laboratory actually reports. It is \
one statistic among several, not the whole record: being second order and \
phase-insensitive, it reveals the frequency and decay of the coherent motion \
but not the state, and it discards everything in the record's higher moments. \
Define an estimator that, for each lag, correlates the record with a shifted \
copy of itself and subtracts the squared mean:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoPointCorrelation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"data_", ",", " ", "hmax_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt_", " ", ":", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"steps_", " ", ":", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "data", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ave", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "data", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "vec1", ",", " ", 
       "mm", ",", " ", "corr"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vec1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"data", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", 
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "hmax"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"data", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "i"}], " ", ";;", " ", 
            RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "hmax", " ", "+", " ", "i"}]}], "]"}],
           "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "hmax", ",", " ", "steps"}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"corr", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "n"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"mm", " ", ".", " ", "vec1"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ave", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"If", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dt", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", "corr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "hmax", ",", " ", "steps"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
          " ", "corr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[54]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One detail of the estimator governs everything below: its lags are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "hmax", ",", " ", "steps"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],
 ", starting at one step, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],
 ", and never reaching ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],
 ". The shot noise is ",
 StyleBox["white", "TI"],
 ", so its autocovariance is concentrated at exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],
 " and vanishes at every other lag. Since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 " is never plotted, the shot noise contributes nothing to the estimate, and \
the raw correlation shows the signal's own structure with no filtering at \
all. Correlate the raw current out to a lag of eight time units:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"corrRaw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"twoPointCorrelation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"current", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"8", "/", "\[Delta]tc"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc", ",", 
     " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[55]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot it against the lag ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "corrRaw", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<two-point correlation C(\[Tau])\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The raw current's correlation oscillates at the Rabi \
frequency\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The correlation falls from its largest plotted value at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],
 " and oscillates as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],
 ": the first trough sits near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 " and the first peak near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "1.8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 ", which is the Rabi period ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[TildeTilde]", "1.8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],
 ". There is no spike at the origin, precisely because the estimator skips ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],
 " where the white shot noise lives. The oscillation amplitude decays on the \
scale of the emission time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "\[TildeTilde]", "1.4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 ", and past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "2.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 " the later cycles sink into the estimator's statistical scatter, a few ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 " over a finite record. So the raw record already carries the coherent \
dynamics, but the time-domain correlation fixes the frequency only roughly. \
The clean read is the spectrum, below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],

Cell["Low-Pass Filtering a Shot-Noise Record", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A natural next instinct is to denoise the current with a low-pass filter, \
and it is worth seeing what that does to a shot-noise-dominated record, \
because the result is easy to misread. Shot noise is ",
 StyleBox["white", "TI"],
 ": its power is flat in frequency out to the sampling limit. A low-pass of \
cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],
 " keeps only the frequencies below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],
 ", discarding most of the noise power, but it also ",
 StyleBox["colors", "TI"],
 " what survives, giving the filtered noise a correlation time of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 ". The zero-lag spike is then no longer a spike: it is smeared into a bump a \
few ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Times]", "1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 " wide. Define a zero-phase Butterworth low-pass (forward then reversed, \
averaged, so features are not shifted in time):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"butterworthFilter", "[", 
    RowBox[{"data_", ",", " ", "\[Omega]c_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt_", " ", ":", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"order_", " ", ":", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "f", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ToDiscreteTimeModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ButterworthFilterModel", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Lowpass\>\"", ",", " ", "order", ",", " ", 
            "\[Omega]c"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
       "   ", 
      RowBox[{"f", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RecurrenceFilter", "[", 
        RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "data"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RecurrenceFilter", "[", 
        RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "data", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"f", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "b", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Correlate the filtered current the same way, at cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "50"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 ", so the filter's correlation time is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "0.02"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],
 ", two steps:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"corrSmooth", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"twoPointCorrelation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"butterworthFilter", "[", 
      RowBox[{"current", ",", " ", "50", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"8", "/", "\[Delta]tc"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc", ",", 
     " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],

Cell["\<\
Measure the small-lag values against the raw correlation's largest:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"corrRaw", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"corrSmooth", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"corrSmooth", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
     RowBox[{"corrRaw", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[59]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The filtered correlation starts near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"9", "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 ", about nine times the largest value the raw correlation ever reaches, and \
it falls back to the oscillation's amplitude within a few lags (below a tenth \
of its height by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.13"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 "). That short-lag feature, a bump a few ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Times]", "1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 " wide, is why a plot of ",
 Cell[BoxData["corrSmooth"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],
 " is dominated by the origin and buries the oscillation. It is not the Rabi \
signal. The test is to run the identical filter on a pure Wiener record of \
the same length with no qubit at all:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pureNoise", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Delta]tc", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "current", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"corrNoise", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"twoPointCorrelation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"butterworthFilter", "[", 
      RowBox[{"pureNoise", ",", " ", "50", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"8", "/", "\[Delta]tc"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc", ",", 
     " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"corrSmooth", ",", " ", "corrNoise"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<filtered current\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<filtered pure noise\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<two-point correlation C(\[Tau])\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The small-lag bump is the filter acting on shot noise, not the \
qubit\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two bumps coincide: filtering pure noise reproduces almost all of the \
feature (about ninety percent of its height), and the pure-noise curve is \
flat past it, while only the current keeps an oscillation at larger ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 ". The bump is the filter, not the qubit. To see what the filter does to the \
actual signal, plot both correlations again with the bump excluded, \
restricting the lag to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0.2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pastBump", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ">=", " ", "0.2"}], " ", 
        "&"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"corrRaw", ",", " ", "corrSmooth"}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"pastBump", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<raw current\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Butterworth-filtered\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<two-point correlation C(\[Tau])\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Past the bump the filter tracks the same oscillation, more \
smoothly\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Past the bump the filtered correlation traces the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 " as the raw one, with the high-frequency scatter removed, so the first Rabi \
cycle reads more cleanly. That is the honest accounting: the low-pass \
suppresses jitter at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[GreaterTilde]", "0.2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " at the price of a spurious bump at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[LessTilde]", "0.13"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],
 ", and it does ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " strip the noise and leave the signal clean. The raw correlation needed \
none of this, since the estimator already skips the lag where the shot noise \
sits. A low-pass earns its place when the ",
 StyleBox["current itself", "TI"],
 " must be smoothed, for a display or a feedback loop, not as a way to read \
the correlation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell["The Power Spectrum: What the Experiment Reports", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],

Cell["\<\
The frequency-domain view is the clean one. By the Wiener-Khinchin theorem \
the power spectrum of the current is the Fourier transform of its two-point \
correlation, and it separates signal from noise where the time-domain \
correlation cannot: white shot noise, flat in frequency, becomes a constant \
floor, while the coherent oscillation becomes a peak on top of it, at the \
Rabi frequency and with a width set by the emission rate. Estimate it by \
Welch's method, averaging the periodograms of many segments of the record so \
the floor comes out smooth:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"powerSpectrum", "[", 
    RowBox[{"data_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "nseg_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "seglen", ",", " ", "segs", ",", " ", "half", ",", " ", "psd", ",", " ",
        "freqs"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"seglen", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "data", "]"}], "/", "nseg"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"segs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
        RowBox[{"data", ",", " ", "seglen"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"half", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
        RowBox[{"seglen", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"psd", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"dt", "/", "seglen"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"#", " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], 
             "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "segs"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"freqs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"seglen", " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"seglen", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"freqs", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", "half"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"psd", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", "half"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[62]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute it and plot over a band that brackets the drive, marking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 " with a gridline:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"spectrum", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"powerSpectrum", "[", 
      RowBox[{"current", ",", " ", "\[Delta]tc", ",", " ", "120"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", "8"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"spectrum", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\[CapitalOmega]c", "}"}], ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency \[Omega]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<power spectrum S(\[Omega])\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The homodyne spectrum peaks at the Rabi frequency\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[63]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spectrum is flat at the shot-noise floor away from the drive and rises \
to a peak right at the gridline, about a factor of two above the floor here, \
modest because the measurement is weak and sharper the harder one drives or \
the longer one averages. Three numbers come straight off it: the peak ",
 StyleBox["position", "TI"],
 " is the Rabi frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 ", the peak ",
 StyleBox["width", "TI"],
 " is the emission rate, and the ",
 StyleBox["floor", "TI"],
 " is the detector's shot noise. Read the peak position off the data, with no \
knowledge of the Hamiltonian that produced it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"MaximalBy", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
     RowBox[{"spectrum", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "<=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"#", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", "5"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", " ", "Last"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[64]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "3.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 " to the frequency resolution of the estimate, about ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.19"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 " here. Fitting the peak's width instead gives the emission rate, which is \
continuous-measurement spectroscopy, and the point is that the coherent \
motion the earlier Bloch plots showed is present here too, now read from the \
record alone, which is all an experiment ever has."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],

Cell["Are the Earlier Trajectories Real, or Is Only the Record?", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the question Part I set up and Part VI has to answer. Only the \
record is measured. The conditional state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 ", and every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 ", purity, and Bloch vector plotted from a single run in Parts III through \
V, was ",
 StyleBox["inferred", "TI"],
 " from a record, never read off a meter. So were those single-run plots a \
fiction?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell["\<\
No, and it is worth being precise about why. The conditional state is the \
observer's best estimate of the system given the record, and the SME is \
exactly the machine that computes it, the optimal quantum filter, the quantum \
analogue of a Kalman filter. An estimate is not a fiction, and this one is \
tied to measurable quantities three ways.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First, the inferred state predicts the record's own measurable statistics. \
The mean current is an observable, a number you get by averaging the readout; \
the inferred trajectory predicts it as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],
 " times the conditional signal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 " averaged along the run. Compare the two:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<mean current, measured off the record:    \>\"", ",", " ", 
       
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "current", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<\[Delta]t \[Times] mean inferred signal Tr[(L+L\[Dagger])\
\[Rho]c]:   \>\"", ",", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Delta]tc", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Lc", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"Lc", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".", 
              " ", "#"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Most", "[", "trajC", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
   "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[65]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "They agree to the shot-noise floor: the current the detector produced is, \
on average, exactly what the inferred trajectory says it should be, and the \
spectral peak above is the same statement in frequency, the record's coherent \
frequency sitting where the inferred state oscillates. Part VI reproducing \
these record statistics ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " a test of the inferred trajectory, and it passes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second, averaging the inferred conditional quantities over many runs gives \
the unconditional master-equation state, and ",
 StyleBox["that", "TI"],
 " is directly measurable, by repeating the experiment and averaging: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 " averaged over runs equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],
 ". Parts III and V computed exactly this, the mean of two hundred \
conditioned trajectories falling on the independent ",
 Cell[BoxData["LindbladSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],
 " curve to the Monte-Carlo scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 ". That agreement tests the inference against a quantity an experiment \
measures without ever reconstructing a single trajectory."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Third, laboratories reconstruct ",
 StyleBox["and verify", "TI"],
 " the single conditional trajectory. Continuous-measurement optomechanics \
runs this same filter on the photocurrent in real time: a levitated \
nanoparticle (Magrini et al., Nature 595, 373 (2021)) and a soft-clamped \
membrane (Rossi et al., with the companion \"Observing and verifying the \
quantum trajectory of a mechanical resonator\", Phys. Rev. Lett. 123, 163601 \
(2019)) each reconstruct the conditional state from the record by a real-time \
Kalman filter and check its predictions against the measured data."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],

Cell["\<\
So the single-run conditional quantities are not fake. They are inferences, \
testable through the record statistics they predict and through the ensemble \
averages that are directly measurable, and they are reconstructed and \
verified in the laboratory. What they are not is a raw meter reading: they \
are the best estimate conditioned on one record, and when detection is \
inefficient (Part VII) even the best estimate is mixed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],

Cell["What Else a Record Gives You", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state, the spectrum, and the mean current are a few uses of a record, \
not all of them. With the whole record in hand, the ",
 StyleBox["future", "TI"],
 " readings also constrain the state at an earlier time, and combining past \
and future gives a strictly sharper estimate, the quantum ",
 StyleBox["smoother", "TI"],
 ". The record, or the state filtered from it, can drive the Hamiltonian in \
real time to stabilize, cool, or error-correct the qubit, which is quantum \
feedback, the setting the positivity-preserving scheme was built for, since a \
filter that returned a non-state would feed the controller nonsense. And the \
correlation and spectrum are only second order: the higher moments, the full \
distribution of a time-integrated current, and, for a photon-counting rather \
than homodyne record, waiting-time distributions and antibunching all come \
from the same stream. The filter itself is a free choice matched to the \
question, the Butterworth low-pass above merely denoising, a ",
 StyleBox["matched", "TI"],
 " filter tuned to detect a specific feature, a ",
 StyleBox["lock-in", "TI"],
 " pulling out one quadrature at the drive frequency, and a ",
 StyleBox["Wiener", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Kalman", "TI"],
 " filter giving the statistically optimal estimate. The record is the raw \
observable; the state, its spectrum, the system's parameters, and a feedback \
signal are all things one computes from it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],

Cell["Part VII: What the Dimension-General Map Unlocks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 " takes plain matrices of any size and carries the detector efficiency \
honestly, and both facts open doors a qubit-only, unit-efficiency version \
cannot. Take efficiency first. Real detectors lose some of the signal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 ", so part of the emitted information escapes unrecorded. The conditioned \
state then no longer purifies: it is a genuine mixture, its Bloch vector \
shrinks inside the sphere, yet the ",
 StyleBox["ensemble", "TI"],
 " average is unchanged, because the unconditional master equation never knew \
there was a detector. Set a driven, emitting qubit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]e", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"He", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]e", " ", 
    RowBox[{"X", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]e", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Le", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]e", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0e", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]te", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfe", " ", "=", " ", "8.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[66]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],

Cell["Run one trajectory at unit efficiency:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"runFull", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Rho]0e", ",", " ", "He", ",", " ", "Le", ",", " ", "\[Delta]te", ",",
        " ", "tfe"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[67]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell["Run one at half efficiency, on the same seed:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"runHalf", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]0e", ",", " ", "He", ",", " ", "Le", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]te", ",", " ", "tfe"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[68]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[69]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],

Cell["Compare the mean purity of the two runs:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<mean purity at \[Eta] = 1:   \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", "runFull"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
    ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<mean purity at \[Eta] = 0.5: \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", "runHalf"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[70]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At unit efficiency the conditioned states stay essentially pure (purity \
near ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 "): a perfect record leaves the observer certain of the state. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],
 " the mean purity drops well below ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],
 ", because half the information leaks away and the best inferred state is \
mixed. See it geometrically: draw the sphere with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"BlochSpherePlot", "[", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],
 " and overlay both full trajectories, the unit-efficiency run and the \
half-efficiency run:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<BlochSpherePlot\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", "runFull"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", "runHalf"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "420"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[71]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full-efficiency curve rides on the surface of the ball; the \
half-efficiency curve stays inside it, its shrunken radius the visible \
signature of unrecorded information. Yet both, averaged over many runs, \
return the same Lindblad state, since the ensemble average is independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],
 ". That ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],
 "-independence of the average, together with the correct handling of the Ito \
correction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"c", "o", "r", "r"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 ", is exactly the content the efficiency factor carries."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now dimension. Nothing in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],
 " mentions the number ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],
 ", so a qutrit runs by the same call. Build the spin-1 lowering operator, a \
soft drive from it, and its emission channel, with the excited ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],
 " as the initial state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Jm3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}],
      ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";",
   " ", 
  RowBox[{"Sx3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"Jm3", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "Jm3", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"H3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1.5", " ", "Sx3"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"L3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.6", "]"}], " ", "Jm3"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]03", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Delta]t3", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf3", " ", "=", " ", "8.0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[72]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one qutrit trajectory at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"run3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]03", ",", " ", "H3", ",", " ", "L3", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0.4", "}"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]t3", ",", " ", "tf3"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[73]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm the states are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],
 " and every one is positive semidefinite:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<state dimension: \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", 
        RowBox[{"First", "@", "run3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<all physical? \>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Tally", "[", 
        RowBox[{"PositiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", " ", "/@", " ", "run3"}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[74]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The states are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],
 " and physical: the same positivity guarantee holds in any dimension. \
Confirm the physics too, that the ensemble mean reproduces the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "=", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],
 " master equation. Set the grid:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tgrid3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]t3", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tf3", "/", "\[Delta]t3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[75]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Solve the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "=", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],
 " master equation with the same ",
 Cell[BoxData["LindbladSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lind3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"H3", ",", " ", "L3", ",", " ", "\[Rho]03", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tf3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[76]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],

Cell["Run 200 qutrit trajectories:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ens3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "9", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]03", ",", " ", "H3", ",", " ", "L3", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0.4", "}"}], ",", " ", "\[Delta]t3", ",", " ", "tf3"}],
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "200", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[77]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],

Cell["Read the three level populations off a state:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"pop3", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[78]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],

Cell["Collect the ensemble-mean populations over time:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanPops", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"pop3", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "ens3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[79]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],

Cell["Collect the master-equation populations over time:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lindPops", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"pop3", "[", 
       RowBox[{"lind3", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     "tgrid3"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[80]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the ensemble means (solid) against the master equation (dashed):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tgrid3", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", "meanPops"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tgrid3", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", "lindPops"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Black"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"SwatchLegend", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Black"}], "}"}], ",",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<|1\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<|0\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",",
         " ", "\"\<|-1\:27e9 mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Lindblad (all three)\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<level populations\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A qutrit at \[Eta] = 0.4: 200 trajectories average to the d = 3 \
master equation\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[81]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],

Cell["\<\
The three level populations of the ensemble mean land on the three \
master-equation curves. This is the payoff of building the integrator on \
plain, dimension-general matrices with an explicit efficiency: inefficient \
detection and higher-dimensional systems are the same function call, not a \
rewrite, and both stay physical and correct in the mean.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],

Cell["\<\
Before we close, let us summarize the most important points we have computed \
and checked:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The stochastic master equation is the Lindblad master equation plus one \
innovation term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", "\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],
 " per monitored channel, and the detector emits ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The positivity-preserving update writes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],
 " as a normalized sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],
 " terms, so every conditioned state is positive semidefinite at any step \
size, which we confirmed with ",
 Cell[BoxData["PositiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "=", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Averaging many trajectories reproduces the master equation to the \
Monte-Carlo scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],
 ", for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],
 " dephasing, for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],
 " emission, and for the qutrit."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Strong ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],
 " monitoring freezes the qubit (the quantum Zeno effect, decay at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],
 "), while weak monitoring lets Rabi oscillations survive with a slow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],
 " decay."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],

Cell["\<\
Only the record is directly measured; the conditional state and every Bloch \
vector or purity plotted from a single run is inferred from it, the SME \
acting as the optimal filter.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],

Cell["\<\
The power spectrum of the homodyne current is flat at the shot-noise floor \
and peaks at the Rabi frequency (its width the emission rate), which is how \
the coherent dynamics are read from the record; the small-lag bump in the \
Butterworth-filtered time-domain correlation is filtered shot noise, not \
signal, as filtering pure noise confirms.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],

Cell["\<\
A record supports more than a spectrum: state filtering (what the Bloch plots \
are), parameter estimation, smoothing, and feedback, with the choice of \
filter set by the question.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],
 " the conditioned state is mixed and its Bloch vector sits inside the \
sphere, while the ensemble average stays ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],
 "-independent and equal to the master-equation state."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for continuously \
measured quantum systems: the stochastic master equation and its readout, a \
positivity-preserving map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],
 " over plain matrices of any dimension, the Function Repository's ",
 Cell[BoxData["LindbladSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],
 " as the master-equation reference and ",
 Cell[BoxData["BlochSpherePlot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],
 " for the sphere, exercised on dephasing, spontaneous emission, the homodyne \
current's spectrum, inefficient detection, and a qutrit. The single most \
consequential parameter is the ratio of measurement rate to internal \
dynamics: turn it up and the record pins the state and freezes coherent \
motion; turn it down and the state follows its Hamiltonian, barely disturbed. \
The natural continuations are quantum feedback, using the conditioned state \
or the record to drive the Hamiltonian in real time (the setting the scheme \
was built for), and larger monitored systems, two qubits and beyond, where \
the same dimension-general call runs unchanged and the trajectories carry \
entanglement conditioned on a shared record."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],

Cell["Acknowledgment", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The qubit examples follow the continuous-measurement lectures of Gabriel T. \
Landi and the homodyne-trajectory pictures of Wiseman and Milburn's ",
 StyleBox["Quantum Measurement and Control", "TI"],
 "; the integrator implements the positivity-preserving scheme cited in Part \
II. The framing throughout, one conditioned run against the average of many, \
is the trajectory unravelling that makes an abstract master equation into \
something an experiment records."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
